2026-09-20 syncfs design correction; goals remain IN_PROGRESS.

The recent census diagnosis is sound but its proposed one-file syncfs patch is not. https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/534 was CLOSED UNMERGED as incorrect, not superseded. Its preserved Codex and actual Claude reviews found two P2 failures that a naive host syncfs forwarding path would recreate: synthetic proc descriptors reopened O_PATH were forced to success instead of native EBADF, and regular synthetic proc memfds lose semantic identity after queued SCM_RIGHTS plus closure of every sender alias, after which host syncfs targets the private backing memfd/filesystem and can falsely succeed. Public closure: https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/534#issuecomment-5628233615. Verified closure evidence is under worktrees/slots/liteinst-session-recovery/target/reverie-emergency-drain/prs/534/closure, comment SHA-256 cec70882da19b50a612f65b2fb52e58a0a4833c557472051b2fd8fcff1e4bcf1.

Current Reverie preserves proc_files metadata across dup, reopen, fork, exec, and CLONE_FILES, and reidentifies the real /proc root on SCM_RIGHTS receive, but it cannot recover regular synthetic-proc identity from the received kernel right once sender aliases are gone. GuestFileIdentity, fd-number lookup, pathname, memfd name, weak-only state, or an immortal retained fd do not prove the needed identity/lifetime. Therefore the first post-PR608 syncfs work must be a separately reviewed semantic-descriptor-transfer prerequisite, followed by the actual syncfs dispatch/refusal/helper/tests. A kernel-carried self-authenticating design must prove guest unforgeability and ABI transparency; a userspace ledger must cover STREAM/DGRAM boundaries, partial sends, ordering, MSG_PEEK, MSG_CTRUNC, recvmmsg, rollback, teardown, aliases, and fd reuse. If neither design clears that bar, stop the implementation rather than silently narrowing syncfs.

After that prerequisite, syncfs must use low-32-bit fd decoding, preserve exact host errno, return EBADF for synthetic proc O_PATH, avoid every host syncfs call for usable synthetic proc and fdinfo carriers, and preserve ordinary read-only descriptor behavior. Tests must combine real proc, synthetic regular proc, forged same-name memfd, all sender aliases closed before receive, retransmission, and an EIO interposer that proves which path called the host. The unchanged backend-parity-c/fsync-durability cell must move from sync ok=5 of 6 to 6 of 6 and then produce strict BitwiseInfoV1 matched evidence with nonzero compared INFO counts before any L2 claim.

Policy conflict: current Hermit AGENTS.md requires that strict KVM evidence; the older backend-reality-reviewer skill says KVM logs are unavailable and never L2. Follow current AGENTS.md and current source. Process deviation retained: the read-only planner invoked safehermit --help, which ran no guest/build/test but created wrapper evidence run_id 20260921T010830Z-1982569 under parent ignored/safehermit, outside its NONE write boundary. The evidence was preserved; no source/ref/TaskGraph/GitHub state was changed by that worker.
